# Web testing

Overlaps `.cursor/rules/testing.mdc`; pair with **`.cursor/rules/typescript/testing`** for unit/spec files next to UI code.

## CI vs manual / harness

**GitHub Actions (default):** `go test`, `tsc --noEmit`, web build, no-Radix, lean **`e2e/`** smoke (health, setup+login API, one sign-in heading). No layout screenshots, axe, or Lighthouse in CI unless a Feature rubric explicitly requires it.

**Manual / Feature harness:** visual, a11y, perf, and breakpoint checks below — when product risk warrants it, not on every push.

## Priority ladder (manual / harness — not default CI)

### 1. Critical journeys

Auth, setup, API contracts — covered by unit tests + lean Playwright API smoke.

### 2. Visual regression (optional)

Playwright screenshots at **320, 768, 1024, 1440** only when a wireframe or design HTML is the AC — not a standing gate on every PR.

### 3. Accessibility

Automated axe plus **manual keyboard** when UI ships materially new surfaces.

### 4. Performance smoke

Meaningful pages vs targets in **`web/performance`** when rubric requires it.

### 5. Cross-browser / responsive

Spot checks before release — not CI matrix by default.

## E2E example (deterministic waits)

```ts
import { test, expect } from "@playwright/test";

test("landing hero renders", async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto("/");
  await expect(page.locator("h1")).toBeVisible();
});
```

Prefer **locators + assertions** instead of brittle fixed **`waitForTimeout`**.

## Unit layer

Exercise pure utilities + hooks logic; brittle DOM snapshots rarely beat visual diff for churny marketing UI-but keep **coverage** commitments from the repo **testing** rule.

Harmonize with **`frontend-evaluator`** rubric breakpoints when harness mode is active.
